WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.647
A claimed shortcut

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:02.095
for one of

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:03.392
cryptography's hardest

00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:04.017
problems

00:00:04.542 --> 00:00:05.190
In a new

00:00:05.002 --> 00:00:05.768
preprint

00:00:06.051 --> 00:00:07.631
researchers from Zhejiang

00:00:07.443 --> 00:00:08.775
University claim a

00:00:08.587 --> 00:00:10.131
deterministic algorithm

00:00:09.955 --> 00:00:10.874
for the discrete

00:00:10.686 --> 00:00:12.183
logarithm problem that

00:00:11.995 --> 00:00:13.669
runs in subexponential

00:00:13.481 --> 00:00:14.105
time

00:00:14.638 --> 00:00:15.699
The claim covers

00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:16.784
discrete logarithms

00:00:16.596 --> 00:00:17.727
in prime fields

00:00:17.551 --> 00:00:18.635
and on prime

00:00:18.529 --> 00:00:19.873
order elliptic curves

00:00:20.027 --> 00:00:20.770
with a running

00:00:20.581 --> 00:00:21.418
time of p

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.314
to the power

00:00:22.126 --> 00:00:22.904
of little o

00:00:22.716 --> 00:00:23.388
of one

00:00:23.918 --> 00:00:24.531
There is a

00:00:24.343 --> 00:00:25.038
catch

00:00:25.177 --> 00:00:26.250
The result only

00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:27.500
holds if OpenAI's

00:00:27.311 --> 00:00:28.608
October twenty twenty

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:29.752
six Cauchy Hermite

00:00:29.564 --> 00:00:31.061
Boolean tensor contraction

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:32.016
construction holds

00:00:32.146 --> 00:00:33.054
so for now

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:33.301
it is a

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:34.304
conditional claim

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.844
Full story on

00:00:35.655 --> 00:00:36.551
the dashboard
